  "preamble": "Debuccalization of the aspirated velar stop [kʰ] to the glottal fricative [h] removes the oral closure and keeps only the aspiration. In Cantonese the Middle Chinese aspirated initial kʰ- (the 溪 initial) became h- before unrounded vowels, and the vernacular layer of Hakka shows the same outcome. The Prakrit reduction of intervocalic kh to h, pronounced [ɦ], is filed under kʰ > ɦ.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Debuccalization, Lenition",
